2 < 1   "about": "The Jev question sets the authoring tools beside this file ask while a plan is written (ask.ts, gate_jev.ts, jev_checks.ts, through jev.ts's loadQuestions), moved here from factory/questions.json so each file has one reader (#1449). Each set says when it is asked (`when`), who reads it (`reader`), how to turn it off (`rollback`), the keys its reader sends (`state`), where it came from (`provenance`) and whether its readings are calibrated; thresholds live in policy.json beside this file. A question is literal: it names no policy word, and nothing here decides anything. A Jev `null` routes that reading to the set's stated rollback, never to a guess. A reworded question is a different question: its readings mean something else.",
